@startuml
!theme vibrant
scale 2

concise "CPU" as CPU
concise "PWM Wrap IRQ" as PWM_IRQ
concise "Timer Alarm" as ALARM
concise "ADC" as ADC
concise "DMA" as DMA
concise "DMA IRQ" as DMA_IRQ
robust "PWM Counter" as PWM_CNT
digital "Internal PWM (A)" as PWM_INT
digital "External PWM (A)" as PWM_EXT


@0
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU
  <font size=12><b>Initialization Phase</b></font>
  1. `hal_motor_init_pwm()` is called.
     - GPIOs are configured.
     - PWM clock divider and wrap value calculated.
     - PWM slices are configured and enabled.
  2. `hal_motor_init_bemf_adc_dma()` is called.
     - ADC & GPIOs are initialized.
     - DMA channel is claimed and configured.
     - DMA & PWM IRQ handlers are installed.
end note
PWM_CNT is "0"
PWM_INT is 0
PWM_EXT is 1

@20
CPU is "Idle"
note right of CPU
  System is idle, waiting for commands.
end note

@40
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU
  `hal_motor_set_pwm(179)` is called
  (duty_cycle = 70%)
  `on_level` is calculated for 70% duty.
  PWM channel A level is set.
end note

@50
CPU is "Idle"

== Operational Phase: 1x 20kHz Cycle (50µs), 70% Duty Cycle ==

@60
PWM_CNT is "0"
PWM_IRQ is "Active"
CPU is "Active"
note right of PWM_IRQ
  PWM counter reaches 0,
  triggers Wrap Interrupt.
end note
note right of CPU
  `on_pwm_wrap()` ISR begins.
  - IRQ is cleared.
  - Schedules BEMF ADC trigger
    via hardware timer.
end note

@62
PWM_IRQ is "Idle"
CPU is "Idle"

@65
ALARM is "Active"
note right of ALARM
  Timer fires after `adc_trigger_delay_us`
  (e.g., ~5µs into the OFF phase).
  The BEMF measurement must happen
  during the PWM OFF period.
end note
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU
  `delayed_adc_trigger_callback()`
  - Calls `trigger_adc_measurement()`
end note

@66
ALARM is "Idle"
ADC is "Active"
note right of ADC
  ADC is enabled and starts
  free-running sampling.
end note
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU
  `trigger_adc_measurement()`
  - Sets up ADC round-robin.
  - Drains ADC FIFO.
  - Re-arms DMA channel.
  - Starts ADC (`adc_run(true)`).
end note

@67
CPU is "Idle"
DMA is "Transferring"
note right of DMA #lightblue
  For every sample in the ADC FIFO,
  the ADC peripheral asserts the DREQ signal.
  The DMA controller responds instantly,
  transferring one `uint16_t` sample from
  ADC FIFO to the Ring Buffer in RAM.
  This happens `BEMF_RING_BUFFER_SIZE` times.
end note
ADC -> DMA : DREQ
@68
ADC -> DMA : DREQ
@69
ADC -> DMA : DREQ
@70
ADC -> DMA : DREQ

@75
DMA is "Idle"
ADC is "Idle"
DMA_IRQ is "Active"
note right of DMA_IRQ
  DMA completes its transfer count,
  triggers DMA Interrupt.
end note

@76
CPU is "Active"
note right of CPU
  `dma_irq_handler()` ISR begins.
  - Stops ADC (`adc_run(false)`).
  - Clears DMA IRQ flag.
  - Processes BEMF buffer.
  - Calls user callback.
end note

@78
DMA_IRQ is "Idle"
CPU is "Idle"


' --- Corrected PWM Waveforms for one 50µs Phase-Correct Cycle (70% Duty) ---
' 1. PWM Counter (`PWM_CNT`) forms a triangle wave (0 -> TOP -> 0).
' 2. `hal_motor_set_pwm` maps 70% duty to a LOW compare level (`on_level` approx. 30% of TOP).
' 3. Internal PWM is HIGH when Counter < `on_level` (at start and end of cycle).
' 4. External PWM is INVERSE of internal, creating a single, centered HIGH pulse.
' 5. Active time: @67.5 to @102.5 = 35µs. Total cycle: 50µs. (35/50 = 70%).

@60
PWM_CNT is "0"
PWM_INT is 1
PWM_EXT is 0

@67.5 ' 15% into cycle (7.5µs), counter rises above compare level.
PWM_CNT is "500"
PWM_INT is 0
PWM_EXT is 1

@85 ' 50% into cycle (25µs), counter reaches the peak (TOP).
PWM_CNT is "1000"

@102.5 ' 85% into cycle (42.5µs), counter falls below compare level.
PWM_CNT is "500"
PWM_INT is 1
PWM_EXT is 0

@110 ' 100% into cycle (50µs), counter is back at 0.
PWM_CNT is "0"
PWM_INT is 1
PWM_EXT is 0

@enduml
